+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Inert definitions for the transport-layer symbols that the vendor wmt core
+ * links against but which cannot be built on mainline (yet).
+ *
+ * On MT6771 the MT6631 connectivity subsystem is reached over the internal
+ * AXI bus.  The vendor tree also ships SDIO, UART and BTIF transports for the
+ * same core; those files pull in vendor-private headers (mtk_io.h, mtk_lpae.h,
+ * mtk-gic-extend.h, btif platform glue) that mainline does not have.
+ *
+ * Every symbol below belongs to one of those unused transports.  Nothing on
+ * the AXI path calls them, so inert bodies are correct rather than a mask for
+ * a real failure: the goal is to link the core (wmt_core / wmt_ctrl /
+ * wmt_func / wmt_ic_soc) so chip power-up and firmware download can be
+ * exercised.  When a transport is genuinely needed, replace the stub with the
+ * real driver.
+ */
+
